<h1>Set up gallery feed</h1>

<p>
    Add Open VSIX Gallery as an extension source to discover independently published extensions
    and receive updates for extensions you already have installed.
</p>

<section>
    <h2>Get the Open VSIX Gallery extension</h2>
    <p>
        To get automatic updates to installed extensions that publish nightly builds to this website,
        simply install the
        <a href="https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=MadsKristensen.VSIXGallery-nightlybuilds">
            Open VSIX Gallery
        </a>
        extension. It registers the main feed in Visual Studio for you and is the easiest option
        for all Visual Studio editions. Visual Studio Enterprise users can instead choose specific
        feeds with the manual setup below.
    </p>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>Choose the right feed</h2>
    <p>There are several feeds in this gallery you can subscribe to.</p>

    <dl>
        <dt>The main feed</dt>
        <dd>
            By subscribing to the <a href="/feed/">main feed</a> you will be notified by
            Visual Studio whenever a listed extension in this gallery is updated. This is the
            best choice for most users.
        </dd>

        <dt>Feed per author</dt>
        <dd>
            Each author page links to a feed containing that author&rsquo;s listed extensions,
            so you can follow only the publishers you trust.
        </dd>

        <dt>Feed for individual extension</dt>
        <dd>
            Each extension page links to its own feed. Use it when you only want updates for
            one extension.
        </dd>
    </dl>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>Set up a feed manually</h2>
    <p>
        Additional extension galleries are a Visual Studio Enterprise feature. If you use another
        edition, install the extension above instead. In Visual Studio, open
        <strong>Tools &gt; Options &gt; Environment &gt; Extensions</strong>. Under
        <strong>Additional Extension Galleries</strong>, select <strong>Add</strong>.
    </p>
    <ol>
        <li>Enter a descriptive name, such as <strong>Open VSIX Gallery</strong>.</li>
        <li>Enter the feed URL. For the main feed, use <a href="/feed/">https://www.vsixgallery.com/feed/</a>.</li>
        <li>Select <strong>OK</strong> to save the gallery.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
        See Microsoft&rsquo;s
        <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/visualstudio/ide/configure-extension-update-options#add-private-extension-galleries"
           rel="noopener noreferrer">extension gallery documentation</a>
        for the current Visual Studio instructions.
    </p>
</section>
